TU1NZ Commercial S4 runtime evidence grant diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-30
Status: APP FIX MERGED; CONTROL REBINDING IN REVIEW

Finding
-------
The stopped post-merge verification used the dedicated runtime DSN and found
that the role tu1nz_adult_commercial_s3_runtime had no privileges on the two
S4 append-only evidence tables created by migration 0018. Both tables were
empty. The completed two-hour acceptance remained valid because providers were
disabled and the S4 evidence-write path was never exercised.

Correction
----------
Application merge a745540b81a368b2e5f09d1fcdb49342b686ae0e adds reversible
migration 0019. It grants only SELECT and INSERT when the dedicated runtime role
exists. UPDATE, DELETE, TRUNCATE, REFERENCES and TRIGGER remain ungranted. The
bootstrap/prestart gate now counts both S4 tables, rejects every provider
receipt while providers are disabled, and bounds beta metrics to the single
validated synthetic submission context.

Validation
----------
739 unit tests and the complete PostgreSQL 17.11/18.6 acceptance matrix are
green locally and in PR/post-merge CI. The review finding that requested S4
table inclusion in the start-state gate was resolved before merge.

Rollback
--------
Migration 0019 down revokes exactly SELECT and INSERT. It deletes no evidence.
Service start is not part of this correction. The existing S4 recovery point
and stopped/static unit remain the operational rollback boundary.

Safety
------
No provider credential, provider call, real identity data, real payment,
adult media, external publication, open beta or production capability is
introduced or authorized.
